---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import cities from '../../data/cities.json';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Website Audit', href: '/website-audit/' },
  { label: 'Services', href: '/website-audit-services/' },
  { label: 'Locations', href: '/website-audit-services/locations/' },
];

const toc = [
  { label: 'UK Locations', id: 'uk-locations' },
  { label: 'US Locations', id: 'us-locations' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Website Audit Services by Location',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'AuditWeb', url: 'https://auditweb.site' },
  description: 'Website audit services delivered locally across the UK and US, with city-specific market context for each location.',
  areaServed: [...cities.uk.map(c => c.name), ...cities.us.map(c => c.name)],
};
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Website Audit Services by Location"
  description="Find website audit services in your city, covering major UK and US locations from London to Los Angeles. Same audit, local market context."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  schema={schema}
  publishDate="2026-08-26"
>

<p>We deliver the same 72-checkpoint website audit everywhere. The one difference is local market context. Each city page below covers the specific competitive landscape, common issues, and search behaviour we see in that market.</p>

<p>Every city below gets the same audit — see our <a href="/website-audit-services/">full range of audit services</a> for scope and pricing.</p>

<h2 id="uk-locations">UK Locations</h2>

<ul>
  {cities.uk.map(city => (
    <li><a href={`/website-audit-services/${city.slug}/`}>{city.name}</a> — {city.region}</li>
  ))}
</ul>

<h2 id="us-locations">US Locations</h2>

<ul>
  {cities.us.map(city => (
    <li><a href={`/website-audit-services/${city.slug}/`}>{city.name}</a> — {city.region}</li>
  ))}
</ul>

<p>Don't see your city listed? Our audit process works the same way anywhere — <a href="/website-audit-services/">get in touch via the main services page</a> and we'll confirm coverage for your location.</p>

</ContentLayout>
